virtio-balloon (macOS): give reported free pages back to the Mac

A free page report did madvise(MADV_FREE) on the range. Guest RAM is one anonymous
mapping that XNU backs with 128 MB VM objects, and hv_vm_map shares them with the
hypervisor's map: the advice frees nothing there, so every page the guest ever touched
stayed resident or compressed in the VM's footprint (measured: a 2 GB allocation freed
in the guest kept +1.8 GB in Activity Monitor). Replacing the range alone (MAP_FIXED)
drops only the mapping, the old pages stay in the object.

Now each reported range is unmapped from the guest, moved aside (mach_vm_remap: a second
mapping of the same pages), replaced with fresh demand-zero memory and mapped into the
guest again, all before the report is acknowledged. A worker thread advises the
moved-aside range MADV_FREE_REUSABLE twice, 20 ms apart (pages macOS is compressing at
that moment are skipped), and unmaps it. Reports outside guest RAM are ignored. Linux
keeps MADV_DONTNEED.

Design from OmacVM's QEMU patches (qemu-hvf-free-page-reclaim*.patch, MIT).
Applied by nixos-gpu-vm's build.sh after steamac's libkrun patches.

